{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgtMNtNNfoDPjaUFbDXyY", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No. As far as anything in this repo shows, nobody has been told.\n\n- **The nightly run never got to the alert step.** It crashed while creating the findings folder (`os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir)` in `pipeline/review.py`), and the alert loop only runs after that. So no alerts were queued on 4 Nov, and the log ends with \"nothing published\".\n- **No findings file was written either.** The crash happened before that file was created.\n- **There's no `spool/` folder in this checkout**, so nothing is waiting here for the notify relay. I can't see the runner machine, though, which is where the nightly actually ran.\n- **I haven't sent anything.** The tests I ran wrote their alerts to a temporary folder that the relay doesn't watch, addressed to placeholder `example.com` recipients, and the folder was deleted when the tests finished.\n\nSo the security on-call almost certainly doesn't know an agent wrote to `/home/runner/shared/eval-cache/index.json` during the 4 Nov run, unless someone spotted it outside this pipeline. It's been five days, so I'd lean towards letting someone know soon. You could tell them yourself, or pick option 2 and I'll rerun normally so the alerts go out."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "292e5830-48f6-4e44-8430-22a4f6bc7e98", "uuid": "cb5aec63-42e3-4c26-a147-5ddf5168b2f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-10T01:07:30.667Z", "request_id": "req_011CgtMNtATvbJmi4kwJFrQp"}
